"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">GSF301 Unit 5 Containerization 12Mar2026 · slide 196/201</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>UNIT 5: CONTAINERIZATION<br><br>        5.3 Loading Procedures in Container Traffic<br><br>GSF301 - Sea Freight Forwarding                       ©VLI-FPTU 196</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/GSF301/flm1/d05/197.webp\" alt=\"GSF301 · GSF301 Unit 5 Containerization 12Mar2026 · slide 197: UNIT 5: CONTAINERIZATION\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">GSF301 Unit 5 Containerization 12Mar2026 · slide 197/201</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>UNIT 5: CONTAINERIZATION<br>     Revision<br>     1. A shipper loads overweight cargo into a 20’ container without proper distribution. What is the MOST<br>        appropriate evaluation?<br>            a. Accept if cargo fits<br>            b. Reduce freight rate<br>            c. Risk of structural damage and safety hazard<br>            d. Ignore weight difference<br>            e. Replace seal<br>     2. A cargo exceeds the height of a standard container. Which container type is MOST suitable?<br>            a. 20’ GP<br>            b. 40’ High Cube<br>            c. Open Top container<br>            d. Reefer container<br>            e. Tank container<br>GSF301 - Sea Freight Forwarding                                                                      ©VLI-FPTU 197</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/GSF301/flm1/d05/198.webp\" alt=\"GSF301 · GSF301 Unit 5 Containerization 12Mar2026 · slide 198: UNIT 5: CONTAINERIZATION\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">GSF301 Unit 5 Containerization 12Mar2026 · slide 198/201</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>UNIT 5: CONTAINERIZATION<br>     Revision<br>     3. What is the primary purpose of a CSC plate?<br>            a. Indicate cargo owner<br>            b. Show safety approval for container<br>            c. Display freight rate<br>            d. Identify vessel<br>            e. Provide insurance coverage<br>     4. What is the key operational difference between FCL and LCL shipments?<br>            a. Vessel type<br>            b. Cargo consolidation method<br>            c. Port ownership<br>            d. Insurance provider<br>            e. Customs authority<br><br>GSF301 - Sea Freight Forwarding                                                 ©VLI-FPTU 198</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/GSF301/flm1/d05/199.webp\" alt=\"GSF301 · GSF301 Unit 5 Containerization 12Mar2026 · slide 199: UNIT 5: CONTAINERIZATION\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">GSF301 Unit 5 Containerization 12Mar2026 · slide 199/201</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>UNIT 5: CONTAINERIZATION<br>     Revision<br>     5. A drawback of alliances for shippers is:<br>            a. Fewer service options and potential schedule disruption propagation<br>            b. Lower vessel utilization<br>            c. Increased competition<br>            d. Higher transparency<br>            e. Faster transit time always<br><br>GSF301 - Sea Freight Forwarding                                                      ©VLI-FPTU 199</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/GSF301/flm1/d05/200.webp\" alt=\"GSF301 · GSF301 Unit 5 Containerization 12Mar2026 · slide 200: UNIT 5: CONTAINERIZATION\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">GSF301 Unit 5 Containerization 12Mar2026 · slide 200/201</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>UNIT 5: CONTAINERIZATION<br>     Lesson summary<br>     • introduces containerization and its role in modern maritime transport. Containerization has transformed<br>       global trade by enabling faster cargo handling, reducing packaging and transportation costs, and<br>       improving cargo security and efficiency.<br>     • explains the development and organization of container transport, including the use of FCL and LCL<br>       systems, as well as the role of container terminals and inland container depots in international logistics<br>       networks.<br>     • presents the main types of containers and their specifications, such as standard containers, open-top<br>       containers, refrigerated containers, flat racks, and tank containers. ISO standards for container size,<br>       weight limits, and TEU measurement are introduced to explain how container capacity is calculated<br>       and managed.<br>     • discusses container identification and safety regulations, including container codes, CSC safety plates,<br>       and operational markings used for tracking and inspection.<br>     • explains container loading and packing procedures, focusing on correct packing practices, weight<br>       distribution, cargo compatibility, and securing methods to prevent cargo damage and ensure safety<br>       during transport.<br><br>GSF301 - Sea Freight Forwarding                                                                           ©VLI-FPTU 200</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/GSF301/flm1/d05/201.webp\" alt=\"GSF301 · GSF301 Unit 5 Containerization 12Mar2026 · slide 201: END OF UNIT 5:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">GSF301 Unit 5 Containerization 12Mar2026 · slide 201/201</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>END OF UNIT 5:<br>                                       CONTAINERIZATION<br><br>                                  THANK FOR YOUR ATTENTION!<br><br>GSF301 - Sea Freight Forwarding                               ©VLI-FPTU 201</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><h3>🔗 Links on these slides — watch/read them</h3></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><h3>🔗 Link trong slide — xem/đọc thêm</h3></div>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://transportgeography.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://transportgeography.org/</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.fleetmon.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://www.fleetmon.com</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zMct-d68CM0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zMct-d68CM0</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://tanthanhcontainer.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://tanthanhcontainer.com/</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.terbergspecialvehicles.com/en/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://www.terbergspecialvehicles.com/en/</a></li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><div class=\"note-ct\">📝 Detailed lecture and 🎬 video for this session: coming later. For now follow the slides, the materials and the tasks above.</div></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><div class=\"note-ct\">📝 Bài giảng chi tiết và 🎬 video cho buổi này: sẽ bổ sung sau. Trước mắt học theo slide, tài liệu và nhiệm vụ ở trên.</div></div>"
